  "id": "Compound::DB00220 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Nelfinavir and Cyp2b6 are linked through a shared pathway involving Nevirapine, which binds to Cyp2b6. The evidence suggests that Nelfinavir causes physiological effects such as insulin resistance, fat redistribution, and lipodystrophy, all of which are mediated by Nevirapine. These effects are linked to the enzyme Cyp2b6, which is inhibited by Nevirapine. The lowest common ancestor of Nelfinavir and Nevirapine is classified as an Enzyme Inhibitor and an Organic Heteropolycyclic Compound, indicating a common biochemical mechanism. The integration of these pathways suggests that Nelfinavir may indirectly influence Cyp2b6 through its effects on Nevirapine, which in turn binds to the enzyme. This mechanism highlights a potential role of Nelfinavir in modulating Cyp2b6 activity via Nevirapine, emphasizing a complex interplay between the drug and the metabolic pathways it affects.",
